// Import code-actions fixture. Demonstrates the LSP's import management:
// "Remove unused import" / "Add import" quick-fixes plus the
// source.organizeImports and source.fixAll actions. The integration tests drive
// the edits described below and assert that the server returns the documented
// actions.
//
// The file compiles as-is. Each experiment is an edit the test makes before
// asking the server for quick-fixes or source actions. Keep the instruction
// comments above the import block; a comment inside the block makes the
// whole-region source actions decline.
//
//   ADD IO   Delete the `std/io` line. `io.print` and `io.inspect` go
//            undefined -> "Add import std/io" / fixAll re-adds it as a
//            block entry, preserving the import block style.
//   ADD DURATION
//            Delete the `std/duration.Duration` line. `Duration.seconds` goes
//            undefined -> "Add import std/duration.Duration" / fixAll
//            re-adds it as a block entry.
//   REMOVE   Add a line `  std/lists.List` to the block. Unused -> "Remove unused
//            import" / fixAll drops it.
//   FIXALL   Several edits at once, then save with fixAll-on-save: one pass
//            removes the unused imports and re-adds the missing ones.
import {
    std/duration.Duration
    std/io
}

fn main() {
    ["a", "b", "c"]
    |> String.join()
    |> io.print()

    5
    |> Duration.seconds()
    |> io.inspect()
}
